  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Sierra Leone Employers Federation (SLEF) is the oldest employers &#x2018;organization in the country and was a very strong organization before the civil war in Liberia. However, the civil war, Ebola and COVID negatively on its operations and membership. The organisation lost many members, which either ceased operations or were discouraged by its ineffectiveness. The ILO has developed an in intervention to assist SLEF in setting up with a sustainable information and training service on labour laws and social dialogue mechanism.

The focus of the intervention includes policy advice, capacity building and trainings and peer learning. In addition, the ILO will work with tripartite partners to facilitate social dialogue on labour administration.</narrative>
  </description>
